commit 79d3a1ad041c4fcdbbffde0106c0f994faf046a7
Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Thu Oct 8 11:25:00 2026 -0700

    Let the types rule out the missing letter
    
    Undo the test double. Instead of testing that an impossible letter
    throws, make it impossible to write.
    
    getLetterGrade() now returns a LetterGrade, "A" | "B" | "C" | "D" |
    "F", instead of any string. GRADE_POINTS is a Record<LetterGrade,
    number>, which must have a value for every letter, so there's no
    default case left to cover. If someone adds "A+" to LetterGrade and
    forgets its grade points, the code doesn't compile.
    
    The @returns line no longer lists the letters: the type says it, and
    the compiler checks it. Coverage is 100% with no new test.
    
    The other options were to leave the line uncovered, or to tell the
    coverage tool to skip it with an /* istanbul ignore */ comment. Either
    is reasonable for truly defensive code. Coverage is a way to find
    untested behaviour, not a score to max out.

